        {
          "id": "intro",
          "type": "text",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "Most new habits don't fail for lack of willpower. They fail because they ask for too much, too soon.",
          "size": 14.7,
          "lineHeight": 19.2,
          "listLineHeight": 17.64,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "article",
          "type": "text",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "***A habit is easier to keep when it is:***\n\n- **Small.** Two minutes a day is easier to start than twenty.\n- **Tied to something you already do.** After the kettle, before the school run.\n\nStart with one. Keep it for a week, then add the next.",
          "size": 14.7,
          "lineHeight": 19.2,
          "listLineHeight": 17.64,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "highlight",
          "type": "highlight",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "Small and steady beats big and rare.",
          "size": 14.7,
          "lineHeight": 19.2,
          "gap": 0,
          "color": "accent",
          "background": "tint",
          "font": "body"
        }
